This project ports the GOAL mode design of OpenAI Codex to the Cursor IDE.

The prompt templates under extracted/ (continuation.md, budget_limit.md,
objective_updated.md) are reproduced from the OpenAI Codex repository
(https://github.com/openai/codex), licensed under the Apache License 2.0.
The architecture notes under extracted/ describe that same codebase
(crate codex-rs/ext/goal).

The Cursor skill under skill/codex-goal/ is a derivative work that adapts
those templates and the goal state machine to Cursor's agent runtime.

The Cursor skill under skill/computer-use/ is a derivative work that
reimplements the Codex Computer Use action space (the @oai/sky full-desktop
API: screenshot/click/move/drag/press_key/scroll/type_text) on Cursor
primitives. The Windows executor scripts/cua.ps1 is original code (Win32
P/Invoke) authored for this project; the action space and naming are from
OpenAI Codex.
